description":"<p><strong>What is the version information for this release?</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Microsoft Edge Version</th>\n<th>Date Released</th>\n<th>Based on Chromium Version</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>152.0.4191.53</td>\n<td>08/28/2026</td>\n<td>152.0.7977.64/.65</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","ordinal":10000}],"revisions":[{"cveNumber":"CVE-2026-69446","version":1,"revisionDate":"2026-08-28T07:00:00-07:00","initialDate":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","description":"<p>Information published.</p>\n","unformattedDescription":"Information published.","notificationNeeded":true,"notificationSent":false,"sourceId":"36a19115-c09c-f111-93a1-000d3ac5fb71"},{"cveNumber":"CVE-2026-69446","version":1.1,"revisionDate":"2026-10-30T07:00:00-07:00","initialDate":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","description":"<p>Corrected CVE by adding the assigning CNA. This is an informational change only.</p>\n","unformattedDescription":"Corrected CVE by adding the assigning CNA. This is an informational change only.","notificationNeeded":false,"notificationSent":false,"sourceId":"52cb519a-85d4-f111-a059-6045bd0a04e8"}]},{"id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-00006664e843","releaseDate":"2026-10-13T07:00:00-07:00","cveNumber":"CVE-2026-97798","cveTitle":"Windows Error Reporting Service Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability","releaseNumber":"2026-Oct","vulnType":"Security Vulnerability","latestRevisionDate":"2026-10-30T07:00:00-07:00","description":"<p>Improper neutralization of argument delimiters in a command ('argument injection') in Windows Error Reporting allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges locally.</p>\n","cweList":["CWE-88: Improper Neutralization of Argument Delimiters in a Command ('Argument Injection')"],"cweDetailsListForSearch":["cwe: CWE-88: Improper Neutralization of Argument Delimiters in a Command ('Argument Injection')","cweUrl: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/88.html"],"unformattedDescription":"<p>Improper neutralization of argument delimiters in a command ('argument injection') in Windows Error Reporting allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges locally.</p>","mitreText":"CVE-2026-97798","mitreUrl":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-97798","publiclyDisclosed":"No","exploited":"No","latestSoftwareReleaseId":1,"latestSoftwareRelease":"Exploitation More Likely","olderSoftwareReleaseId":0,"denialOfService":"N/A","tag":"Windows Error Reporting","issuingCna":"Microsoft","issuingCnaId":100000001,"severityId":100000001,"severity":"Important","impactId":100000002,"impact":"Elevation of Privilege","langCode":"en-US","baseScore":"7.8","temporalScore":"6.8","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H/E:U/RL:O/RC:C","vectorStringSource":"Microsoft","isMariner":false,"customerActionRequired":true,"customerActionRequiredId":1,"cweDetailsList":[{"keys":["cwe","cweUrl"],"values":["CWE-88: Improper Neutralization of Argument Delimiters in a Command ('Argument Injection')","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/88.html"]}],"articles":[{"title":"Windows Error Reporting Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability","articleType":"100000000","description":"<p>Improper neutralization of argument delimiters in a command ('argument injection') in Windows Error Reporting allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges locally.</p>\n","ordinal":10000},{"title":"Windows Error Reporting Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability","articleType":"100000000","description":"<p>Improper neutralization of argument delimiters in a command ('argument injection') in Windows Error Reporting allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges locally.</p>\n","ordinal":10000},{"articleType":"FAQ","description":"<p><strong>What privileges could be gained by an attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability?</strong></p>\n<p>An attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability could gain SYSTEM privileges.</p>\n","ordinal":10000}],"revisions":[{"cveNumber":"CVE-2026-97798","version":1,"revisionDate":"2026-10-13T07:00:00-07:00","initialDate":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","description":"<p>Information published.</p>\n","unformattedDescription":"Information published.","notificationNeeded":false,"notificationSent":false,"sourceId":"be421c8f-1fc3-f111-aaae-6045bd00cd58"},{"cveNumber":"CVE-2026-97798","version":1.1,"revisionDate":"2026-10-30T07:00:00-07:00","initialDate":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","description":"<p>Updated an acknowledgement. This is an informational change only.</p>\n","unformattedDescription":"Updated an acknowledgement. This is an informational change only.","notificationNeeded":false,"notificationSent":false,"sourceId":"35ebb9fa-71d4-f111-a059-7ced8d6e4554"}]},{"id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000f2540ebe","releaseDate":"2026-10-13T07:00:00-07:00","cveNumber":"CVE-2026-105008","cveTitle":"Windows Schannel Spoofing Vulnerability","releaseNumber":"2026-Oct","vulnType":"Security Vulnerability","latestRevisionDate":"2026-10-30T07:00:00-07:00","description":"<p>No cwe for this issue in Windows Schannel allows an unauthorized attacker to perform spoofing over a network.</p>\n","cweList":["CWE-420: Unprotected Alternate Channel"],"cweDetailsListForSearch":["cwe: CWE-420: Unprotected Alternate Channel","cweUrl: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/420.html"],"unformattedDescription":"<p>No cwe for this issue in Windows Schannel allows an unauthorized attacker to perform spoofing over a network.</p>","mitreText":"CVE-2026-105008","mitreUrl":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-105008","publiclyDisclosed":"No","exploited":"No","latestSoftwareReleaseId":2,"latestSoftwareRelease":"Exploitation Less Likely","olderSoftwareReleaseId":0,"denialOfService":"N/A","tag":"Windows Schannel","issuingCna":"Microsoft","issuingCnaId":100000001,"severityId":100000001,"severity":"Important","impactId":100000008,"impact":"Spoofing","langCode":"en-US","baseScore":"9.0","temporalScore":"7.8","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H/E:U/RL:O/RC:C","vectorStringSou